\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Solving a graph source equation}
\date{2026-11-10}

\p{The energy identity in \ref{fdip-0008} measures squared
differences of a real field along weighted edges. Adding a positive
multiple of the squared counting norm also penalizes nonzero constant fields.
When does this make the source equation solvable for every source,
and how can the response to a source at one vertex determine the
response to an arbitrary field?}
